    <h2 class="phpdocumentor-content__title">Updater for Composer-based Applications</h2>

    <p class="phpdocumentor-summary">A self-update CLI command for any application managed with
    <a href="https://getcomposer.org/">Composer</a>.</p>

    <p>Add the plugin to your application, and your users can list, download and install any of its versions with a
    single command: <code>composer app:upgrade</code>. The new version's dependencies are installed, the application's
    own upgrade tasks are run, and if anything goes wrong, the previous version is restored automatically.</p>

    <ul>
        <li><a href="guides/developers/index.html">Developer Guide</a>: add the self-updater to your application</li>
        <li><a href="guides/users/index.html">User Guide</a>: upgrade an application which comes with the self-updater</li>
    </ul>

    <p>This application follows the highest coding standards of <a href="https://psalm.dev/">Psalm</a>,
    <a href="https://phpstan.org/">PHPStan</a>, <a href="https://phpmd.org/">PHP Mess Detector</a>,
    <a href="https://github.com/PHPCSStandards/PHP_CodeSniffer/">PHP_CodeSniffer</a>, and complies to
    <a href="https://www.php-fig.org/psr/psr-12/">PSR-12</a> code style guidelines to make sure it is reliable,
    maintainable and easily reusable. It is covered by unit and integration tests with
    <a href="https://phpunit.de/">PHPUnit</a>.</p>

